## Proton Conduction
Hydrogen-Bonded Organic Frameworks (HOFs): A New Class of Porous Crystalline Proton-Conducting Materials $\mathsf{H}^{+}$ conduction: Two porous hydrogenbonded organic frameworks (HOFs) based on arene sulfonates and guanidinium ions exhibit ultra-high proton conductivity (s) $0.75\times10^{-2}{\mathsf{S c m}}^{-1}$ and $1.8\times$ $10^{-2}\mathsf{S c m}^{-1}$ under humidified conditions. They also have very low activation energies and higher proton conductivity at ambient conditions compared to other porous crystalline materials, such as MOFs and COFs.
